<article class="env-example" id="26144B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/26144B">Example <span data-tag="26144B">1.2.14.1</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be the free higher category generated by a single object $X$ and a single morphism $f: X \rightarrow X$. Then $\calC $ is a finitely presented $\infty $-category with a single object, and $\Hom _{\calC }(X,X) = \{  1, f, f^2, \ldots \} $ is infinite and discrete. In particular, we note that the finite presentation of $\calC $ does not guarantee finiteness properties of the morphism spaces. </p>
